# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 8 (a widget application is transparent; `<-` binds the child's result by a tuple pattern), Type System ch. 2 ("Bundles") and ruling TC (places counted as built: the caller's label is 1 after the one-place clause, 2 after the two-place clause); the chosen clause's event and hold are the caller's, so the label follows in the click's tick (as sem-ch08-clause-dynamic-result).
test by_ones

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="up")
    1: Ui.Label(text="0 hits, count 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="1 hits, count 1")

test by_tens

